  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BiH Health Sectors Programmatic Development Policy Loan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Health Sectors Programmatic Development Policy Loan for Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH) is to improve the financial sustainability and service delivery quality of health care systems, as well as strengthen regulatory frameworks on environmental management and tobacco control, in support of improved health outcomes in BiH. This program development objective (PDO) is articulated around two mutually reinforcing pillars. The first pillar, improving the financial sustainability of health institutions, aims to address the beginning of the resolution of the stock of arrears in the health sector and help introduce measures that would prevent the generation of new arrears. The second pillar aims to introduce incentives for improved service delivery and stronger primary health care, as well as strengthen regulatory frameworks on environmental management and tobacco control in support of improved health outcomes in BiH.</narrative>
  </description>
